Designed and programmed an interactive, web-based physics simulation engine comparing classical bicycle aerodynamics against a friction-free electromagnetic levitation concept.Physics Modeling: Solved real-time numerical differential equations for drag force ($F_d = \frac{1}{2} \rho v^2 C_d A$), mechanical rolling resistance, gravitational incline vectors, and power output ($P = F \cdot v$).Interactive Engine: Built a live user-controlled environment featuring variable wind speed, air density/altitude settings, and track gradients.Data Telemetry: Developed real-time telemetry plots, visual force vector displays, dynamic wind-tunnel particle flows, and an automated CSV data logging pipeline for empirical research analysis.
